strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_fractional_min_width_parsed_whole_px_2026-11-27, 0, "Style.min_width_px is an integer and there is no milli part: min-width:87.5px floors to 87px. In an exact-overflow flex row (two width:88px items, margin:0 3.3% in 200px; the first has min-width:87.5px) Chrome freezes the first item at 87.5px; head freezes it at 87px."
    web_fractional_min_width_parsed_whole_px_2026-11-27, 1, "Chrome 159 (first item, blue): k=1 47..133, k=4 186..535. Head at 60e24d81a52: k=1 47..133, k=4 186..533. Needs a min_width milli field (like margin_l_milli) consumed by flex_zero_basis_floor_w and the min-width floor in row flex placement."
    web_fractional_min_width_parsed_whole_px_2026-11-27, 2, "Minimal repro (body{margin:0}, .w{margin-left:40px;width:200px;height:30px}, 400x300, measure blue run on CSS row 10): <div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"min-width:87.5px;width:88px;margin:0 3.3%;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div><div style=\"width:88px;margin:0 3.3%;height:20px\"></div></div>"

